{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558861703,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf551e3ffe3ZNaVzqVUnVWuj","part":{"partID":"prt_1d40b2068001oDPlVh4Lb0BLSR","sessionID":"ses_e2bf551e3ffe3ZNaVzqVUnVWuj","messageID":"msg_1d40b158d001HZXAslXcPXiuXm","type":"tool","id":"call_01_d4fXSKfL0l3TNAI9kCLj0860","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md","offset":50,"limit":50},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md, lines 50-81\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n54: \n55: The argument failure wording, the doctor target list, the per-leg result table, result templates and next-step text live only in `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`.\n56: \n57: ---\n58: \n59: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n60: \n61: The workflow prints the doctor target list.\n62: It then runs seven read-only legs once: the sk-code setup battery, the sk-git setup battery, the trigger index freshness check, the runtime mirror check, the advisor status probe with `--warm-only` and the embedder check, which reads the semantic lane and the command vectors, and the delivery check, which reads whether each runtime's prompt hook is wired and whether Codex has approved it.\n63: The delivery leg reports DEGRADED, never FAIL, when a prompt hook is missing or the Codex hook is unapproved, and names the repair.\n64: It reports each leg as passing, skipped, degraded or failing.\n65: For a failing leg, it names the runnable doctor command that repairs it.\n66: The sk-git leg passes `--tool=<name>` for the AI tool running the command.\n67: Its exit 3 (an unknown check or a gate saved off) is degraded, not failing.\n68: After the legs, it shows the last session hop from the session-relaunch hop history.\n69: It shows an open-notes line while any handoff note is still unclaimed.\n70: It shows the Claude context window the relaunch nudge measures against, or the two settings that supply one when none is configured.\n71: It shows an orphans line from `orphan-process-check.cjs --summary`.\n72: That line counts leftover helper processes and model servers whose launcher died.\n73: These lines are informational and never change the status.\n74: It writes nothing in the repository and never starts the advisor daemon.\n75: The only write outside the repository is the advisor CLI creating its socket directory when that directory is absent.\n76: The default socket directory is `/tmp/system-skill-advisor`.\n77: The advisor leg reports PASS when exit 0 has `data.freshness` set to `live`.\n78: It reports DEGRADED when exit 0 has any other freshness value and names `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.\n79: It reports FAIL when exit 75 includes `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON and names `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`.\n80: It reports SKIP when exit 75 lacks that field because the daemon is stopped.\n81: It reports FAIL for any other exit with `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md, lines 50-81\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n54: \n55: The argument failure wording, the doctor target list, the per-leg result table, result templates and next-step text live only in `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`.\n56: \n57: ---\n58: \n59: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n60: \n61: The workflow prints the doctor target list.\n62: It then runs seven read-only legs once: the sk-code setup battery, the sk-git setup battery, the trigger index freshness check, the runtime mirror check, the advisor status probe with `--warm-only` and the embedder check, which reads the semantic lane and the command vectors, and the delivery check, which reads whether each runtime's prompt hook is wired and whether Codex has approved it.\n63: The delivery leg reports DEGRADED, never FAIL, when a prompt hook is missing or the Codex hook is unapproved, and names the repair.\n64: It reports each leg as passing, skipped, degraded or failing.\n65: For a failing leg, it names the runnable doctor command that repairs it.\n66: The sk-git leg passes `--tool=<name>` for the AI tool running the command.\n67: Its exit 3 (an unknown check or a gate saved off) is degraded, not failing.\n68: After the legs, it shows the last session hop from the session-relaunch hop history.\n69: It shows an open-notes line while any handoff note is still unclaimed.\n70: It shows the Claude context window the relaunch nudge measures against, or the two settings that supply one when none is configured.\n71: It shows an orphans line from `orphan-process-check.cjs --summary`.\n72: That line counts leftover helper processes and model servers whose launcher died.\n73: These lines are informational and never change the status.\n74: It writes nothing in the repository and never starts the advisor daemon.\n75: The only write outside the repository is the advisor CLI creating its socket directory when that directory is absent.\n76: The default socket directory is `/tmp/system-skill-advisor`.\n77: The advisor leg reports PASS when exit 0 has `data.freshness` set to `live`.\n78: It reports DEGRADED when exit 0 has any other freshness value and names `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.\n79: It reports FAIL when exit 75 includes `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON and names `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`.\n80: It reports SKIP when exit 75 lacks that field because the daemon is stopped.\n81: It reports FAIL for any other exit with `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\", \"offset\": 50, \"limit\": 50}"},"time":{"start":1794558861416,"end":1794558861703}}}}
