{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558899512,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf551e3ffe3ZNaVzqVUnVWuj","part":{"partID":"prt_1d40bb259001A5j0cjQ4CNf5MO","sessionID":"ses_e2bf551e3ffe3ZNaVzqVUnVWuj","messageID":"msg_1d40ba0dc0016H8lPNvwIyBw8L","type":"tool","id":"call_fa1360bdd19e4d408ebd3206","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG|SPECKIT_[A-Z_]+\" .skilled/commands/doctor | head -20","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-env-presentation.txt:111:For a section 5 `SPECKIT_SKIP_*` gate, add:\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-deep-loop.yaml:193:      - \"When scope includes research or review, run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-source-tags-helper.mjs <active-spec-folder>. Group its WARN lines by lineage (the folder after research/lineages/ or review/lineages/, or 'main' for the packet's own research or review files) and count each class: gone, moved, past end, guessed. Keep every moved tag's new path. A SKIP line means the packet was created on or before the cutoff: report the reason, never as clean; only when the operator asks to audit an older packet, rerun with SPECKIT_SOURCE_TAG_CUTOFF=2000-01-01. Exit 2 is reported with stderr.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-hook-gates.cjs:10:// pre-push hooks has a SPECKIT_SKIP_* variable, but a variable lasts one command.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-hook-gates.cjs:18:// (SPECKIT_ALLOW_REMOTE_PUSH, SPECKIT_ALLOW_MASS_DELETION) are marked\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:28:  invariant: \"Every leg runs in its check-only form. This route MUST NOT regenerate the trigger index, sync a runtime mirror, start the advisor daemon, install hooks or provision the tree. A failing leg prints the doctor command that repairs it; repair is an explicit operator action, never a side effect of this diagnostic. The one write outside the repository is the advisor CLI creating its socket directory, /tmp/system-skill-advisor unless SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR names another, when that directory is absent. No leg makes it on purpose.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:59:    - \"Leg advisor: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only. Exit 0 with data.freshness set to live is PASS. Exit 0 with any other freshness is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. Exit 75 with a staleDistWarning field in stderr JSON is FAIL, with repair npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is not running. Any other exit is FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status. When data.hookHealth is absent, show hook health not recorded: the prompt hook writes its health records only when SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG is set. It never changes the leg's status.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-git-hooks.yaml:25:  if its SPECKIT_SKIP_* variable were set. Command-line config never counts. gates.tsv\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-git-presentation.txt:105:   remotePush, massDeletion   per-push approvals: set SPECKIT_ALLOW_REMOTE_PUSH=1 or\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-git-presentation.txt:106:                              SPECKIT_ALLOW_MASS_DELETION=1 on that one git push only\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-env.yaml:115:    Show the one-command usage form from the presentation contract, using the variable's documented one-command context where available. Never ask for a value, save the switch, or write it to any file. For a secret per-invocation variable, keep the value placeholder redacted. For a section 5 SPECKIT_SKIP_* gate, point to /doctor:git hooks, which saves a lasting gate setting in git config; this command still writes nothing for it.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt:85:The orphan line is informational only and never changes the doctor status. A model server kept on purpose with `SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_ORPHAN_REAP=0` also shows as unsupervised, so do not reap it. With no orphan processes, print `orphans: none`. Run the listed `--reap` command to see each process, then use its confirmation command with `--yes` only when those are the processes to stop.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs:170:  process.env.SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL = '1';\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs:171:  delete process.env.SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON;\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs:172:  delete process.env.SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_SHADOW_WEIGHTS_JSON;\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs:173:  delete process.env.SPECKIT_ADVISOR_BM25_LEXICAL_SHADOW;\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-code-setup-check.cjs:358:      const flag = process.env.SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING;\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-code-setup-check.cjs:363:          `served the legacy stub because SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=${JSON.stringify(flag)} switches compiled routing off`,\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-code-setup-check.cjs:365:          'unset SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING, then rerun node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-code-setup-check.cjs',\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs:91:const WORKTREE_ENV_REPAIR = 'export SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE=<writable dir>, or unset SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE';\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs:630:  const envValue = process.env.SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE || '';\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-env-presentation.txt:111:For a section 5 `SPECKIT_SKIP_*` gate, add:\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-deep-loop.yaml:193:      - \"When scope includes research or review, run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-source-tags-helper.mjs <active-spec-folder>. Group its WARN lines by lineage (the folder after research/lineages/ or review/lineages/, or 'main' for the packet's own research or review files) and count each class: gone, moved, past end, guessed. Keep every moved tag's new path. A SKIP line means the packet was created on or before the cutoff: report the reason, never as clean; only when the operator asks to audit an older packet, rerun with SPECKIT_SOURCE_TAG_CUTOFF=2000-01-01. Exit 2 is reported with stderr.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-hook-gates.cjs:10:// pre-push hooks has a SPECKIT_SKIP_* variable, but a variable lasts one command.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-hook-gates.cjs:18:// (SPECKIT_ALLOW_REMOTE_PUSH, SPECKIT_ALLOW_MASS_DELETION) are marked\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:28:  invariant: \"Every leg runs in its check-only form. This route MUST NOT regenerate the trigger index, sync a runtime mirror, start the advisor daemon, install hooks or provision the tree. A failing leg prints the doctor command that repairs it; repair is an explicit operator action, never a side effect of this diagnostic. The one write outside the repository is the advisor CLI creating its socket directory, /tmp/system-skill-advisor unless SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR names another, when that directory is absent. No leg makes it on purpose.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:59:    - \"Leg advisor: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only. Exit 0 with data.freshness set to live is PASS. Exit 0 with any other freshness is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. Exit 75 with a staleDistWarning field in stderr JSON is