{"type":"text","timestamp":1794558961320,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf551e3ffe3ZNaVzqVUnVWuj","part":{"id":"prt_1d40c9cd5002OKBTdfmhjNYMnl","sessionID":"ses_e2bf551e3ffe3ZNaVzqVUnVWuj","messageID":"msg_1d40c76b4001rCUk8faw8LmlMu","type":"text","text":"**Files written:** `.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md` — one line appended after the advisor leg lines in section 6:\n\n```\nWhen the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded and names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`, the setting that turns the records on.\n```\n\n**Verify output (both run from the repository root):**\n\n```\n$ rg -c \"hook health not recorded\" .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\n1\n$ rg -c \"/tmp/system-skill-advisor\" .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\n1\n```\n\nBoth match the expected values. The scoped diff is exactly one added line, and `git status --short` for the file shows only ` M .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md`.\n\n**Notes:** I set `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` in backticks, matching the file's treatment of code identifiers elsewhere (`data.freshness`, `staleDistWarning`, `--warm-only`, `/tmp/system-skill-advisor`). The verify regexes and the pending contract test's `/SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG/` assertion match either way. I did not run that contract test (`doctor-setup-contract.test.cjs`), because T034 names only the two `rg` checks and T037 is the task that reruns it. I did not tick the T034 checkbox, and I touched no other file.","time":{"start":1794558958805,"end":1794558961320}}}
